## 3. Step-by-Step Emergency Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | Arrival | Walk-in, ambulance, or referral arrival; verify or quick-register patient. | Reception / Triage nurse |
| 2 | Case opened | Emergency case created with chief complaint and priority. | Triage nurse / Clinician |
| 3 | Triage | Vitals, acuity, isolation flags, routing decision recorded. | Triage nurse |
| 4 | Stabilization | Emergency response, treatment, monitoring documented. | Emergency clinician |
| 5 | Diagnostics / orders | Lab, radiology, medication as needed â" orders on case or linked encounter. | Clinician |
| 6 | Handoff decision | Destination: OPD, IPD, ICU, Theater, referral, or discharge from ED. | Emergency clinician |
| 7 | Handoff execution | `POST /emergency-cases/:id/handoff` orchestrates downstream flow. | System / Clinician |
| 8 | Case closure | Terminal handoffs close case; show deep links to receiving module. | System |

---

## 4. Handoff Destinations

| Destination | Backend orchestration | Receiving module |
| ----------- | --------------------- | ---------------- |
| `OPD` | `startEmergencyOpdFlow` | [opd-flow](./opd-flow.mdc) â" `WAITING_VITALS`, emergency context |
| `IPD` | `startEmergencyIpdFlow` | [ipd-flow Â§2.1](./ipd-flow.mdc) â" deferred billing optional |
| `ICU` | `startEmergencyIcuFlow` | [icu-flow Â§4.1](./icu-flow.mdc) â" IPD + ICU stay |
| `THEATER` | `startEmergencyTheatreFlow` | [theater-flow Â§4.2](./theater-flow.mdc) |
| `REFERRAL` | Case closed with referral note | External â" no IPD |
| `DISCHARGE` | Case closed | Patient leaves from ED |

**Rules:**

- After handoff, surface **Open in OPD / IPD / ICU / Theater** on case detail when links exist.
- Do not recreate IPD from Emergency when patient already routed OPD â' `ADMITTED`.
- Quick registration patients prompt **Complete registration** link to patient registry.

