## UI, access, and quality standards

- Reuse components from `frontend/lib/shared/` before creating module-specific UI; prioritize reusability and consistency.
- Responsive layouts for mobile, tablet, and desktop; keep UI uniform, simple, and intuitive.
- High performance worklists (pagination/lazy lists); localize all user-facing text with concise, clinically appropriate terminology; no raw enum codes in production UI.
- Theme tokens only (`frontend/.cursor/design-system.mdc`); no hard-coded color, spacing, or typography values.
- Strict RBAC+ABAC: menus, components, API endpoints, and workflow actions must never be visible or accessible to unauthorized users. Effective permissions = union(role/module/user grants) ∩ active subscription package ∩ ABAC scope.
- Mutations: optimistic Riverpod update on HTTP success; WebSocket reconciliation (`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`).
- Reference entities by `human_friendly_id` in frontend and API responses; backend maps to internal IDs. Never expose raw table IDs.

